{"id": "EUVD-2026-86929", "enisaUuid": "c7b80ffa-a0c5-3097-bcc7-995de587591f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv6: mcast: use rcu_assign_pointer() for __rcu list updates\n\nSeveral places in net/ipv6/mcast.c update RCU-protected lists\n(np->ipv6_mc_list, idev->mc_list, idev->mc_tomb) using direct pointer\nassignments instead of rcu_assign_pointer():\n\n1. In __ipv6_dev_mc_dec(), unlinking a group from idev->mc_list did:\n       *map = ma->next;\n   without rcu_assign_pointer() while concurrent readers traverse\n   idev->mc_list locklessly under rcu_read_lock().\n2. In ipv6_sock_mc_drop() and __ipv6_sock_mc_close(), unlinking a group\n   from np->ipv6_mc_list directly assigned *lnk = mc_lst->next and\n   np->ipv6_mc_list = mc_lst->next without rcu_assign_pointer(), racing\n   with lockless readers in inet6_mc_check().\n3. In __ipv6_sock_mc_join(), mc_lst->next was initialized to\n   np->ipv6_mc_list via raw assignment before publishing mc_lst.\n4. In mld_del_delrec() and __ipv6_dev_mc_inc(), __rcu source pointers\n   passed into rcu_assign_pointer() lacked explicit dereference helpers.\n\nFix these by consistently using rcu_assign_pointer() along with\nmc_dereference() / sock_dereference().", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:24:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e3e3cec28c4d1bf29948da40b4e9e5d44f7852b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49d7e1b456ba2f3ee08b3e264d999c09992cde8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/afca229b39acc2590976b3e4f6e0fe76cededc60", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e46b0c9fcf7e10b64ce1630b925f47918d1f7f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c8f56c583c3250408367880c98e4d6fbc929315"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98099", "GHSA-5fxh-xwwm-73v4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "110995ba-20ca-347a-a3c0-8195f1cbc334", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "456b61bca8ee324ab6c18b065e632c9a8c88aa39 <0c8f56c583c3250408367880c98e4d6fbc929315"}, {"id": "30cd2576-9952-3151-966e-a8a9b2d41a11", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "456b61bca8ee324ab6c18b065e632c9a8c88aa39 <0e3e3cec28c4d1bf29948da40b4e9e5d44f7852b"}, {"id": "3a302eb7-5a87-3b71-bee7-e89d13275523", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.38"}, {"id": "49445bdb-1472-3107-8680-448d778a45cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "5cdb6208-0c2e-3844-a3b2-3bb7ddd03b5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8e026411-48ce-37cc-871e-e164edac0ede", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "927ca05c-d459-3ee6-9325-59030b1a85b0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "456b61bca8ee324ab6c18b065e632c9a8c88aa39 <afca229b39acc2590976b3e4f6e0fe76cededc60"}, {"id": "9ab3ca11-fd6b-3591-a476-f089cc50dc44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "456b61bca8ee324ab6c18b065e632c9a8c88aa39 <49d7e1b456ba2f3ee08b3e264d999c09992cde8e"}, {"id": "aefb6f22-d434-3497-b727-74ee1dd3de8a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c1504ddb-510c-32e3-b269-2fabd9763b1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "456b61bca8ee324ab6c18b065e632c9a8c88aa39 <2e46b0c9fcf7e10b64ce1630b925f47918d1f7f6"}, {"id": "d75ae88c-50a8-31c0-8ec8-1788685a38d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "e554a7a7-2713-31c2-a74a-4149e000ba15", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "93915499-8291-3559-b550-878543a33edc", "vendor": {"name"